1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,728
Venice is sinking.

2
00:00:01,778 --> 00:00:08,233
This extraordinary city built on water is slowly losing its fight against the sea.

3
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:11,950
It sits inside a shallow lagoon on Italy's Adriatic coast,

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,642
spread across more than a hundred islands,

5
00:00:14,692 --> 00:00:18,167
with three narrow inlets connecting it to the open sea.

6
00:00:18,217 --> 00:00:19,119
Waterlogged,

7
00:00:19,169 --> 00:00:21,975
oxygen-poor mud preserves the piles,

8
00:00:22,025 --> 00:00:25,227
but anaerobic bacteria still attack wood.

9
00:00:25,277 --> 00:00:30,067
Slow decay and the wood-water-soil system maintain stability.

10
00:00:30,117 --> 00:00:32,060
But the sediment keeps compacting.

11
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:36,984
Industrial groundwater pumping accelerated the sinking until the nineteen seventies.

12
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:38,274
In nineteen sixty-six,

13
00:00:38,324 --> 00:00:41,967
a record surge reached one hundred and ninety-four centimetres.

14
00:00:42,017 --> 00:00:43,396
So Italy built MOSE:

15
00:00:43,446 --> 00:00:47,469
seventy-eight hollow steel gates that rest on the seabed,

16
00:00:47,519 --> 00:00:51,900
then swing upward on compressed air to hold the Adriatic back.

17
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:54,632
The shield has held back major tides.

18
00:00:54,682 --> 00:00:56,330
But Venice still sinks,

19
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,807
the sea still rises,

20
00:00:57,857 --> 00:00:59,800
and this city is not alone.

